t appear to be captured in the academic papers and analyses returned by this search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013Kgvyzk6NEUhNd7tsGeanW","session_id":"347907fb-725a-460a-a196-d1b396a4fd53","uuid":"abb4bb2d-67b2-49f6-98e7-2df8453fd605","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:19:58.171Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01395U7EDLhyTDhoQ3fc92go","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ICLR 2026 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ICLR Workshop 2026 - Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://sites.google.com/view/icbinb-2026/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"📈 ICLR 2026 Submission Storm: 19,797 Papers, New Review Rules, and the Age of AI Convergence | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/169/iclr-2026-submission-storm-19-797-papers-new-review-rules-and-the-age-of-ai-convergence\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Author Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/AuthorGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.15462\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Area Chair Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/AreaChairGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Which Coauthor Should I Nominate in My 99 ICLR Submissions? A Mathematical Analysis of the ICLR 2026 Reciprocal Reviewer Nomination Policy\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.17950\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2026 Peer Review FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2026/PeerReviewFAQ\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about ICLR 2026 reviewer guidelines and scoring criteria:\n\n## Scoring Criteria\n\nNumerical scores are provided for soundness, presentation, contribution, confidence, and overall rating. The overall rating for ICLR 2026 is mapped to {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10}.\n\nAdditionally, the new formula reviewers adopt is: Novelty × Depth × Presentation × Reproducibility ≈ Weak Accept+\n\n## Reviewer Expectations\n\nYour reviews are timely and substantive. You follow the reviewing guidelines. You must also adhere to the Code of Ethics in your role as a reviewer and the Code of Conduct.\n\nThe official ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide indicates that Area Chairs, Senior Area Chairs and the Program Chairs will rely greatly on your expertise and your diligent and thorough reviews to make decisions on each paper.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013Kgvyzk6NEUhNd7tsGeanW","session_id":"347907fb-725a-460a-a196-d1b396a4fd53","uuid":"7360f1ff-5865-41c6-af1f-7d865325c45c","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:19:58.564Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PYZCPgshyrfK3zHN49r6Dk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ICLR official reviewer rating scale 1-10\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"📈 ICLR 2026 Submission Storm: 19,797 Papers, New Review Rules, and the Age of AI Convergence | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/169/iclr-2026-submission-storm-19-797-papers-new-review-rules-and-the-age-of-ai-convergence\"},{\"title\":\"Introducing Review Rank: Calibrated Scores and Relative ...\",\"url\":\"https://cspaper.org/articles/introducing-review-rank\"},{\"title\":\"What Have We Learned from OpenReview?\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.05885\"},{\"title\":\"Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.15462\"},{\"title\":\"[Literature Review] Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoonlight.io/en/review/insights-from-the-iclr-peer-review-and-rebuttal-process\"},{\"title\":\"Does double-blind peer-review reduce bias? Evidence from a top computer   science conference\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2101.02701\"},{\"title\":\"Analyzing the Machine Learning Conference Review Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.12919\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 - Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.pangram.com/reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, the ICLR reviewer rating scale has evolved over time:\n\n**Current ICLR Rating Scale (2024-2025):**\nThe overall rating for ICLR 2024 and 2025 is a discrete number in {1, 3, 5, 6, 8, 10}.\n\n**Previous Scales:**\n- For ICLR 2017-2019, reviewers gave a review score (integer) from 1 to 10\n- For ICLR 2020, reviewers gave a rating score in {1, 3, 6, 8}\n\n**Upcoming Change for ICLR 2026:**\nThe new 2–4–6–8–10 system removes the middle ground, forcing reviewers into decisive opinions.\n\nSo rather than a traditional 1-10 scale, ICLR has been using discrete rating sets to limit the options available to reviewers, with the current system using {1, 3, 5, 6, 8, 10} and a planned shift to {2, 4, 6, 8, 10} for ICLR 2026.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013Kgvyzk6NEUhNd7tsGeanW","session_id":"347907fb-725a-460a-a196-d1b396a4fd53","uuid":"68188773-2d90-4fd9-b5e4-2deb56536784","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:19:58.692Z"}
