{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N8kDh8zY8kKCD37HhWPw93","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the provided document, **the specific reviewer rating scale and scoring dimensions for ICLR 2026 are not detailed in this Reviewer Guide.**\n\nThe guide explains the reviewing process and emphasizes that reviewers should \"clearly state your initial recommendation (accept or reject)\" with supporting arguments. However, it does not specify:\n\n- A numerical rating scale (e.g., 1-5, 1-10)\n- Particular scoring dimensions or categories\n- How to assign confidence scores\n\nThe document focuses instead on the four key questions reviewers should answer: What problem is tackled? Is the approach well-motivated? Do results support claims? What is the significance?\n\nFor the actual rating scale and dimensions, reviewers would need to consult the OpenReview submission platform directly, as that information is not included in this guide."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013Kgvyzk6NEUhNd7tsGeanW","session_id":"347907fb-725a-460a-a196-d1b396a4fd53","uuid":"0eeb832e-6af9-4b7f-aa26-90fde2a4ad90","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:20:05.334Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015z1Ztqoy2Y8qKgd5U9FkJK","type":"tool_result","content":"# ICLR 2025 Reviewer Rating Scale\n\nBased on the provided documentation, **the official ICLR 2025 reviewer rating scale and specific scoring dimensions are not detailed in this guide.**\n\nThe document focuses on the reviewing process and expectations rather than numerical ratings or categorical scoring dimensions. It instructs reviewers to:\n\n- Answer four key evaluation questions about the paper\n- Provide an initial recommendation as either \"Accept or Reject\"\n- Engage in discussion phases that may lead to updated recommendations\n\nThe guide emphasizes that reviewers should evaluate whether submissions \"bring sufficient value to the community and contribute new knowledge,\" but it does not specify a formal rating scale (such as 1-5 or 1-10 points) or predefined scoring categories/dimensions for ICLR 2025.\n\nFor the actual rating scale used on the OpenReview platform, you would need to consult the submission system directly or contact ICLR through their official channels."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013Kgvyzk6NEUhNd7tsGeanW","session_id":"347907fb-725a-460a-a196-d1b396a4fd53","uuid":"f6aa44ac-8029-4336-b42f-1b30dbcbb8cf","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:20:06.240Z"}
