{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Y8kCpP7JS4Jq78vhJVqgU","type":"tool_result","content":"# ICLR 2024 Reviewer Rating Scale\n\nBased on the provided content, **the specific reviewer rating scale and scoring dimensions are not detailed in this document**. \n\nThe guide explains the reviewing process and structure, including that reviewers should:\n\n- \"Answer four key questions for yourself, to make a recommendation to Accept or Reject\"\n- Provide an \"initial recommendation (accept or reject) with one or two key reasons\"\n\nHowever, the document does not specify a numerical rating scale (such as 1-10), specific scoring categories, or dimensional scoring criteria that reviewers must use when evaluating papers.\n\nThe guide focuses on the qualitative assessment process rather than quantitative scoring metrics. For the actual rating scale details, reviewers would likely need to consult the OpenReview platform directly or supplementary materials not included in this reviewer guide."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013Kgvyzk6NEUhNd7tsGeanW","session_id":"347907fb-725a-460a-a196-d1b396a4fd53","uuid":"4e1fd946-0cf1-4d71-9220-fd32a850077e","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:20:29.035Z"}
