{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U9YDxtrvCipuAqhy9moLv4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"ICLR\" \"soundness\" \"presentation\" \"originality\" \"significance\" reviewer score\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.15462\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397780200_Insights_from_the_ICLR_Peer_Review_and_Rebuttal_Process\"},{\"title\":\"[Literature Review] Are the confidence scores of reviewers consistent with the review content? Evidence from top conference proceedings in AI\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoonlight.io/en/review/are-the-confidence-scores-of-reviewers-consistent-with-the-review-content-evidence-from-top-conference-proceedings-in-ai\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines – ECML PKDD 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.ecmlpkdd.org/organisation/reviewer-guidelines/\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2026 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2025 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2023 Reviewer Tutorial\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerTutorial\"},{\"title\":\"What Makes a Scientific Paper be Accepted for Publication?\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2104.07112\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about ICLR reviewer scores for soundness, presentation, originality, and significance:\n\n## ICLR Review Scoring Criteria\n\nNumerical scores are provided for soundness, presentation, contribution, confidence, and overall rating. The overall rating for ICLR 2024 and 2025 is a discrete number in {1, 3, 5, 6, 8, 10}.\n\n## Correlation with Overall Rating\n\nThe overall rating correlates most strongly with contribution, then soundness. Additionally, the overall rating shows a positive correlation with the word count of the strengths section and a negative correlation with the word count of the weaknesses section.\n\n## Review Structure\n\nEach submission is typically reviewed by three to five reviewers, who provide structured written feedback along with numerical scores and questions for the authors.\n\nNote: While the search results confirm that ICLR uses soundness and presentation as formal scoring categories, the results indicate ICLR uses \"contribution\" as a score rather than separate scores for \"originality\" and \"significance.\" However, originality and significance are concepts that are evaluated within the contribution assessment, as mentioned in research about peer review practices.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013Kgvyzk6NEUhNd7tsGeanW","session_id":"347907fb-725a-460a-a196-d1b396a4fd53","uuid":"9b961999-8ce8-4ed2-8b55-4ecbc0054687","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:20:37.262Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JJMrcxpCBFmaU3xPYTPFD6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ICLR reviewer rating scale definitions weak reject borderline accept\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.15462\"},{\"title\":\"WHAT DRIVES PAPER ACCEPTANCE? A PROCESS- CENTRIC ANALYSIS OF MODERN PEER REVIEW\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"},{\"title\":\"📈 ICLR 2026 Submission Storm: 19,797 Papers, New Review Rules, and the Age of AI Convergence | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/169/iclr-2026-submission-storm-19-797-papers-new-review-rules-and-the-age-of-ai-convergence\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397780200_Insights_from_the_ICLR_Peer_Review_and_Rebuttal_Process\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2017 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2017/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis of Reviews for CVPR 2012 Aditya Khosla Derek Hoiem Serge Belongie\",\"url\":\"https://people.csail.mit.edu/khosla/papers/reviewer_analysis.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Association between author metadata and acceptance: A feature-rich,   matched observational study of a corpus of ICLR submissions between 2017-2022\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2211.15849\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about ICLR's rating scales, though the results primarily show ICML's detailed scale definitions rather than ICLR's specific definitions.\n\nFrom the ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions (which uses a similar scale to ICLR):\n\n**Weak Accept**: Technically solid, moderate-to-high impact paper, with no major concerns with respect to evaluation, resources, reproducibility, ethical considerations.\n\n**Borderline Accept**: Technically solid paper where reasons to accept outweigh reasons to reject, e.g., limited evaluation.\n\n**Borderline Reject**: Technically solid paper where reasons to reject, e.g., limited evaluation, outweigh reasons to accept, e.g., good evaluation.\n\n**Reject**: For instance, a paper with technical flaws, weak evaluation, inadequate reproducibility and incompletely addressed ethical considerations.\n\nThe search results also indicate that ICLR divides papers into three groups based on average reviewer scores: High-Score (>6), Borderline (5-6), and Low-Score (<5).\n\nIt's worth noting that ICLR 2026 has moved away from the classic 1–5 scale, introducing a new 2–4–6–8–10 system.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013Kgvyzk6NEUhNd7tsGeanW","session_id":"347907fb-725a-460a-a196-d1b396a4fd53","uuid":"d99b3ad2-2170-437a-8a3a-977696fe6425","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:20:37.422Z"}
